{"summary":"The crowned eagle, also known as the African crowned eagle or the crowned hawk-eagle (Stephanoaetus coronatus) is a large bird of prey found in sub-Saharan Africa; in Southern Africa it is restricted to eastern areas. Its preferred habitats are principally riparian woodlands and various forests. The crowned eagle is the only extant member of the genus Stephanoaetus. A second species, the Malagasy crowned eagle (Stephanoaetus mahery) became extinct after humans settled on Madagascar.","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephanoaetus coronatus","cells":[[-18.3,34.8,1],[-17.0,27.1,1],[-17.6,31.3,1],[-15.6,35.5,1],[-18.3,32.0,1],[-17.6,34.1,1],[-18.3,31.3,1],[-16.3,34.8,1],[-18.3,32.7,1],[-15.6,34.8,2],[-18.3,35.5,1],[-20.3,28.5,1],[-19.0,34.8,1],[-19.0,32.7,1],[-19.0,34.1,1],[-34.0,22.1,2],[-32.8,28.5,1],[-32.2,25.7,1],[-31.7,29.2,1],[-24.2,31.3,1],[-26.1,31.3,1],[-34.0,25.0,1],[-24.8,32.0,1],[-22.9,31.3,1],[-34.0,24.3,1],[-28.6,30.6,1],[-34.0,22.9,1],[-29.8,29.9,1],[-29.2,32.0,2],[-28.0,31.3,1],[-29.2,29.9,1],[-27.4,30.6,1],[-32.2,27.1,1],[-28.6,31.3,1],[-33.4,25.0,1],[-26.7,32.7,1],[-29.2,29.2,1],[-22.3,31.3,2],[-26.1,30.6,1],[-32.8,27.8,2],[-28.6,29.9,1],[-32.8,26.4,1],[-33.4,25.7,2],[-24.2,29.9,1],[-32.8,27.1,1],[-28.6,32.7,2],[-26.7,31.3,1],[-25.5,32.0,1],[-33.4,27.1,2],[-34.0,23.6,1],[-24.2,30.6,2],[-31.1,30.6,2],[-26.1,32.0,2],[-33.4,24.3,2],[-23.6,29.9,2],[-22.9,29.2,2],[-22.9,30.6,1],[-22.9,29.9,2],[-32.8,25.7,2],[-25.5,30.6,2],[-33.4,26.4,2],[-34.0,26.4,1],[-28.6,32.0,2],[-29.2,31.3,2],[-31.1,29.9,2],[-24.8,30.6,2],[-29.2,30.6,2],[-22.3,29.9,1],[-25.5,31.3,2],[-29.8,31.3,3],[-28.0,32.7,2],[-27.4,32.0,2],[-27.4,31.3,2],[-28.0,32.0,2],[-26.7,32.0,2],[-29.8,30.6,3],[-24.8,31.3,2],[-30.4,30.6,3]],"months":[88,61,70,100,76,94,105,89,93,74,81,67]}